  "why_correct": "Metformin is withheld around the time of iodinated contrast in patients with significant renal impairment because of the risk of contrast-induced kidney injury and (rarely) lactic acidosis. Renal function is checked before restarting. Patients with normal renal function often need no change.",
  "why_wrong": "A. In renal impairment, precautions are needed with contrast. B. It does not need permanent cessation. C. Lifelong insulin switch is unnecessary. E. Increasing metformin raises the risk.",
  "pearl": "Metformin + contrast + renal impairment → withhold around the scan, recheck renal function before restarting.",
