  "why_correct": "Orthostatic hypotension in an older person is first managed by reviewing contributing medications (antihypertensives, diuretics, alpha-blockers, tricyclics) and non-pharmacological measures (slow position changes, adequate hydration, compression stockings), before considering drugs such as fludrocortisone or midodrine.",
  "why_wrong": "A. Standing quickly aggravates symptoms. B. Bed rest causes deconditioning. C. It is a fall risk, not to be ignored. E. Adding an antihypertensive worsens it.",
