  "correct_answer": "A. Stop the causative drug immediately and admit (burns/dermatology unit)",
  "why_correct": "Stevens-Johnson syndrome / toxic epidermal necrolysis is a life-threatening drug reaction with mucosal involvement and skin detachment. The first and most important action is to stop the causative drug immediately, with urgent admission to a burns or specialist unit for supportive care; delay increases mortality.",
  "why_wrong": "B. Continuing the drug worsens a fatal reaction. C. Topical steroid and discharge are grossly inadequate. D. Antibiotics are not the primary treatment. E. This is a dermatological emergency, not minor.",
  "pearl": "SJS/TEN: STOP the drug now + admit to a burns/specialist unit.",
  "thinking": "New anticonvulsant + mucosal involvement + skin detachment ↓ SJS/TEN ↓ stop drug + urgent admission",
