  "why_wrong": "B. Early contrast CT is for assessing complications/necrosis after 48–72 hours, not first-line for aetiology. C. IgG4 is for suspected autoimmune pancreatitis, a rarer cause. D. MRCP is used if ultrasound is inconclusive, not first. E. Lipids are checked but gallstones are the priority here.",
