  "why_wrong": "B. Sodium is not the principal acute threat. C. Chloride changes are not the danger. D. Hypocalcaemia (not magnesium) can occur but hyperkalaemia is the immediate risk. E. Phosphate rises rather than falls in rhabdomyolysis, and is not the acute killer.",
