  "why_wrong": "A. Alzheimer's is a gradual global decline, not a sudden amnesic state after Wernicke's. B. Delirium tremens is an acute hyperadrenergic withdrawal state, not isolated amnesia. D. NPH gives gait disturbance, incontinence and cognitive slowing. E. Frontotemporal dementia presents with behavioural or language change.",
