  "why_wrong": "A. Praevia causes painless bleeding with a soft, non-tender uterus. B. Vasa praevia causes fetal bleeding at membrane rupture. C. Uterine rupture usually occurs in labour with a scarred uterus and loss of contractions. D. An ectropion causes minor painless spotting.",
