  "presentation": "Kawasaki disease — diagnosis",
  "difficulty": "Moderate",
  "stem": "A 3-year-old has had a high fever for 6 days with bilateral non-purulent conjunctivitis, a strawberry tongue with cracked lips, a polymorphous rash, swollen red hands and feet, and a large cervical lymph node. What is the most likely diagnosis?",
  "options": {
   "A": "Kawasaki disease",
   "B": "Scarlet fever",
   "C": "Measles",
   "D": "Systemic juvenile idiopathic arthritis",
   "E": "Adenoviral infection"
  },
